  "summary": "At a District 10 supervisor candidate forum in San Francisco, frontrunner Theo Ellington said he would not vote to renew SFPD's contract with Flock license-plate readers, a stronger stance than he had previously taken. His top rivals Brookter and Eppler also said they would not extend the Flock contract.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "he indicated he would not vote to renew the San Francisco Police Department's contract with Flock , a license-plate reader tool that has come under intense scrutiny nationwide.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "He previously told Mission Local he would support an expansion of the camera network but with stricter guidelines",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "Brookter and Eppler each said they would ban data centers, restrict billionaire spending in local elections, and not extend SFPD's contract with Flock.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
  ],
